{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>It is a guilt-offering.</b> The Sages and Rabbi Eliezer disagreed (Torat Kohanim ad loc.). The Sages said that <b>הוּא</b> (\"it\") comes to exclude — if he did not slaughter it in the north, it is a disqualification. Rabbi Eliezer says it comes to exclude — if he slaughtered it not for its own sake. Now according to Rabbi Eliezer's reasoning it is precise that <b>אָשָׁם הוּא</b> — the word <b>הוּא</b> refers back to the guilt-offering, teaching that it must be for the sake of a guilt-offering. And although in Zevaḥim (Zevaḥim 10a) we find that Rabbi Yehoshua challenged Rabbi Eliezer, and Rabbi Eliezer went back and derived this law of \"not for its own sake\" from the verse (Leviticus 7:7) <b>כַּחַטָּאת כָּאָשָׁם</b> — since the verse equated them — if so, why is the word <b>הוּא</b> needed? And perhaps it is because without <b>הוּא</b>, I would have said that the equation (hekkesh) comes only regarding the matter of semikhah (leaning), as the Sages expounded there (Zevaḥim 11a); therefore it says <b>הוּא</b> adjacent to <b>אָשָׁם</b>, to say that it must be for the sake of a guilt-offering. And regarding the matter he challenged there, it says <b>כַּחַטָּאת כָּאָשָׁם</b>. And according to the Sages, <b>הוּא</b> comes to exclude slaughter not in the north, which was mentioned in the parashah (verse 2), and it comes to disqualify. And although one could raise objections similar to those that Rabbi Yehoshua raised against Rabbi Eliezer also according to the Sages' view — since they did not innovate a new law through their own reasoning in their exposition, but rather a matter that applies to all offerings, and it is also mentioned explicitly; only, from a single verse I would have said it is not a disqualification — they can derive <b>הוּא</b> as coming for a disqualification. This is unlike Rabbi Eliezer, who produced a new law that has no parallel; therefore all the objections recorded there were raised against him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:53:45.026458264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}